```

```{r averaging-bias, echo = FALSE, fig.width = 9, fig.height = 6.5, out.width = "100%", fig.cap = "**Figure 6.** Relative bias in each toxicity estimate under a fixed equation and under model averaging, on the same 200 simulated datasets per cell. Each segment runs from the fixed-equation result to the averaged result for one approach, with the arrow head at the averaged value; the dashed line is zero bias. A retains the measurements, C left-censors them, B3 floors them and fixes the asymptote at zero, E floors them through a Beta and F through a Gamma. The first two columns share a control coefficient of variation of 9.6% and differ in how far the true curve descends below zero; the third is the same design as the first at a control coefficient of variation of 1.9%."}
ggplot(phase10, aes(y = arm, colour = arm)) +
  geom_vline(xintercept = 0, linetype = "dashed", colour = "grey40") +
